|name = Deathshund
|image = E 744.png
|first appearance = '''CotC''': [[Neptune (Cats of the Cosmos)/Outbreak|Chapter 3 - Neptune Outbreak]]<br>'''ZL''': [[Awash with Spare Keys|Sub-chapter 25 - Awash with Spare Keys]]
|money drop = 900¢ - 3,555¢
}}

==Enemy==
This somewhat fast backliner is very tanky and damaging like its other variants, but acts more like a variant of [[Le'boin]] or [[THE SLOTH]] in practice, delivering punishing Area Attacks from a surprisingly high range of 440, far beyond the reach of many accessible [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] specialists, with any survivors being Frozen for 2 seconds. On top of its singular knockback, it has a distant burrow and revives once with full HP. Fortunately, its longer attack cycle offers windows of opportunity where units can still chip it before the next attack lands and keeps it from pushing as easily as [[Cadaver Bear]].

==Strategy==
You should use [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] to both chip away at its health and serve as a meatshield against it. The best way to handle Deathshund is to take advantage of its slow attack rate and sneak in hits with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] or [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]], with the latter being able to disable its freeze. Without certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]], outranging it is generally never a viable option, as even [[Talents|Talented]] [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] is outranged, and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] only has a tiny effective Long Distance range that lets her hit Deathshund without retaliation (only viable when there is a sizeable amount of peons in front of it).

Always save your [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] for Deathshund in any stage it's in, as it deals a hefty amount of damage and lets you stall Deathshund while gradually chipping at its health pool. From that point you should try and kill it as fast as possible, utilizing even non-[[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to damage it, only making sure that the last hit forces this dog to roll over in its grave.

